# OPERATOR-LOCAL fixture saves (never committed).
#
# A lane whose host needs real DENSITY rather than a shape - the GUI census walks every
# Parsek window and photographs it, and a window with no rows photographs as an empty
# box - names its template under `fixtures/local-saves/<leaf>` and the operator fills it
# from a save he already has:
#
#   python harness/tools/stage_local_fixture.py --from "<KSP>/saves/c1" --as c1-gui
#
# The bytes stay local (tens of MB, and the content is a personal career), so every
# committed suite must stay green with the directory EMPTY - which is what the
# `fixtures/local-saves/` prefix buys: hlib.is_local_fixture_template classifies such a
# template from its path, and the per-spec cells that read a template off disk skip it.
#
# WHY THIS IS NOT A `fixtures/saves/` ENTRY: test_saveparse's committed-set sweep lists
# the DIRECTORIES under fixtures/saves/ and compares them to a pinned set, so a staged
# local fixture there would red that cell on the one machine that can fly the lane.
#
# This file and the README beside it are the only committed contents.
*
!.gitignore
!README.md
